# Shell scripts run on Linux (WSL/EC2/CI) — force LF regardless of the checkout OS. Found
# 2026-07-02: no .gitattributes existed, so a Windows working tree could silently accumulate CRLF
# (git blob stayed clean LF, only the local disk copy was corrupted) — `sh deploy/aws-ec2-test/
# backup.sh` failed with "illegal option -" under WSL until the local files were reset from HEAD.
# This doesn't fix a past commit (there was none to fix), it stops it from ever becoming one.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same reasoning, different extension: user-data.sh.tpl (deploy/aws-ec2-test/terraform) is a bash
# script read verbatim by Terraform's file() into EC2 user_data and executed by cloud-init on
# boot — a CRLF-corrupted copy would break bootstrap silently on the instance. *.sh above doesn't
# match *.sh.tpl, so it needs its own rule.
*.sh.tpl text eol=lf

# .github/scripts/*.py (uptime-alert.yml) run under `python3` in CI (Linux runners) — same
# precautionary rule, cheap insurance against the identical class of bug even though Python's
# tokenizer tolerates CRLF better than a shell shebang does.
*.py text eol=lf

# Snapshot vitest ditulis ULANG dengan LF setiap `npm test`, sementara checkout Windows
# menormalkan ke CRLF — sehingga menjalankan uji SELALU mengotori pohon kerja meski nol
# perubahan isi. Ditemukan 2026-07-27: churn ini memblokir `git checkout`/`git rebase`
# tiga kali dalam satu sesi. Bahayanya bukan gangguannya, melainkan kebiasaan yang
# ditimbulkannya — membuang berkas snapshot "yang biasanya kosong" tanpa melihat adalah
# cara yang bagus untuk suatu hari membuang perubahan snapshot yang SUNGGUHAN.
*.snap text eol=lf
